<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch06-12--gpt> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch06-12: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.57";
    dc:description "Phylogenetic comparative data can quantify inheritance for selected traits and clades. The organism-wide universal and the amount meant by 'chief part' prevent complete resolution.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Partition morphological variation into phylogenetic inheritance and association with current ecology using comparative models across clades. Strong phylogenetic signal after controlling for present habits supports the claim; predominantly ecology-specific structure would oppose it.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "'Chief part' lacks a natural unit of measurement.", "Inheritance and adaptation are not mutually exclusive explanations.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.66"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-12--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-12--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-12--gpt--dataset-3>;
